          "new_text": "def filter_api_calls(\n    logp_with_result: np.ndarray,\n    logp_call_only: np.ndarray,\n    logp_no_call: np.ndarray,\n    tau_filter: float,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return an ordered keep mask and one finite margin per proposed call.\"\"\"\n    # Validate threshold\n    if isinstance(tau_filter, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter cannot be boolean\")\n    if not np.isscalar(tau_filter) or tau_filter < 0 or not np.isfinite(tau_filter):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must be finite nonnegative scalar\")\n    \n    # Validate matrices\n    for arr, name in [(logp_with_result, 'logp_with_result'), (logp_call_only, 'logp_call_only'), (logp_no_call, 'logp_no_call')]:\n        if not isinstance(arr, np.ndarray):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a numpy array\")\n        if arr.ndim != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a 2D matrix\")\n        if arr.shape[0] == 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} cannot be empty\")\n        if not np.all(np.isfinite(arr)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} contains nonfinite values\")\n        if np.any(arr > 0):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} contains positive values\")\n    if not (logp_with_result.shape == logp_call_only.shape == logp_no_call.shape):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input matrices must have the same shape\")\n    \n    n, H = logp_with_result.shape\n    \n    # Compute weights\n    t = np.arange(H)\n    raw_weights = np.maximum(0, 1 - 0.2 * t)\n    weights = raw_weights / raw_weights.sum()\n    \n    # Compute losses\n    L_plus = -np.dot(logp_with_result, weights)\n    L_call_only = -np.dot(logp_call_only, weights)\n    L_empty = -np.dot(logp_no_call, weights)\n    L_minus = np.minimum(L_empty, L_call_only)\n    margin = L_minus - L_plus\n    keep_mask = margin >= tau_filter\n    \n    return keep_mask, margin.astype(float)"
